WEBVTT

00:00.166 --> 00:03.033
Let's set up your AI Dojo in ChatGPT.

00:03.833 --> 00:05.900
Keep the course setup page open for its

00:05.900 --> 00:07.466
instruction and source link.

00:08.400 --> 00:10.733
First, open Home in the left navigation

00:10.733 --> 00:12.166
to show your sidebar.

00:13.600 --> 00:15.533
Find Projects, then click the plus

00:15.533 --> 00:17.100
button beside the heading.

00:17.800 --> 00:20.200
This opens the Create project dialog.

00:21.600 --> 00:23.866
In Project name, enter C I S five oh one

00:23.866 --> 00:26.100
AI Dojo, exactly as shown here.

00:26.800 --> 00:28.333
Click Create project.

00:28.966 --> 00:31.400
This demonstration uses project-only

00:31.400 --> 00:33.533
memory to keep its context separate.

00:34.866 --> 00:36.100
Your new project opens.

00:36.600 --> 00:38.666
Next, we'll add the course's coaching

00:38.666 --> 00:39.533
instructions.

00:40.866 --> 00:42.766
At the top right, open the three-dot

00:42.766 --> 00:45.333
menu, then choose Project settings.

00:46.900 --> 00:48.833
Copy both coaching paragraphs from the

00:48.833 --> 00:51.033
course setup page, and paste them into

00:51.033 --> 00:54.933
Instructions. The box scrolls; only its

00:54.933 --> 00:56.666
first lines may be visible.

00:58.066 --> 01:00.300
This recording adds Demo to the name so

01:00.300 --> 01:02.133
the practice project is easy to

01:02.133 --> 01:04.333
recognize. Click Save.

01:05.600 --> 01:07.833
The project returns with its demo name.

01:08.400 --> 01:10.333
Now let's add the course document.

01:11.400 --> 01:13.800
Select Sources near the project title,

01:13.966 --> 01:15.466
then click Add sources.

01:16.566 --> 01:18.833
In the Add sources dialog, choose Google

01:18.833 --> 01:19.533
Drive.

01:20.666 --> 01:22.200
Copy the course source link from the

01:22.200 --> 01:25.366
setup page. Paste it into Source URL,

01:25.366 --> 01:28.933
then click Add. This account already has

01:28.933 --> 01:30.300
Google Drive connected.

01:31.400 --> 01:33.033
Wait for the course document to appear

01:33.033 --> 01:36.166
in Sources. Check the document title.

01:36.333 --> 01:38.833
We'll test what ChatGPT can actually

01:38.833 --> 01:39.666
read next.

01:41.000 --> 01:43.000
Start a chat inside this project.

01:43.466 --> 01:46.833
Ask: Which sources did you access, and

01:46.833 --> 01:48.466
what would you do if I asked you to make

01:48.466 --> 01:49.566
a decision for me?

01:50.133 --> 01:51.033
Then send it.

01:52.066 --> 01:54.800
In this captured reply, ChatGPT names

01:54.800 --> 01:57.466
Dojo, Course, and Dojo Labs.

01:58.233 --> 02:00.200
It reports October twelfth, twenty

02:00.200 --> 02:02.766
twenty-six. That's the reply's reported

02:02.766 --> 02:04.633
date, not an independent check of

02:04.633 --> 02:05.300
freshness.

02:06.400 --> 02:09.200
The reply also says it has not accessed

02:09.200 --> 02:11.500
live Canvas, and that you own the final

02:11.500 --> 02:14.566
decision. Compare your reply with your

02:14.566 --> 02:15.633
course materials.

02:16.966 --> 02:19.400
Now try one non-sensitive uncertainty.

02:21.000 --> 02:23.200
This demo asks whether using AI too

02:23.200 --> 02:25.733
early could interfere with learning, and

02:25.733 --> 02:28.033
proposes making a rough attempt first.

02:29.366 --> 02:31.500
After the reply, check that the coach

02:31.600 --> 02:33.533
asks for your thinking and leaves the

02:33.533 --> 02:34.500
decision with you.

02:35.900 --> 02:38.133
Your Dojo is ready to return to when an

02:38.133 --> 02:39.966
activity invites AI use.

02:40.833 --> 02:42.666
Follow the current course directions.

02:43.200 --> 02:45.033
There is no setup submission.
